@startuml
!include style.puml
title Multi-agent workflow for one tasks.md item

|Human owner|
start
:Pick a tasks.md item in own ownership lane
(Developer A: Lim-ZY, Developer B: thegrimbee);
|Orchestrator|
:Record goal, owner, source revision and
worktree in workflow/plans/;
|Analyst|
:Explore task-relevant code, specs and prior decisions;
:Write source-linked context brief + candidate edit paths;
:Draft OpenSpec delta (requirements, scenarios)
and list decisions needing a human;
|Human owner|
if (Approve requirements and decisions?) then (no)
  :Revise or stop;
  stop
endif
:Record decisions in design.md;
|Orchestrator|
:Confirm disjoint write paths, dependencies
and parallel worktrees; write handoff;
fork
  |Test-writer|
  :Write tests under tests/ only;
fork again
  |Implementer|
  :Change only assigned source paths;
end fork
|Frontend|
if (Visible UI changed?) then (yes)
  :Read-only rendered-UI inspection
  with current -> desired findings;
else (no)
endif
|Reviewer|
:Read-only review of every acceptance
criterion, quality, security, tests;
if (Findings?) then (yes, at most 2 fix rounds)
  |Implementer|
  :Fix and re-verify;
  |Reviewer|
  :Re-review;
endif
|Orchestrator|
:Consolidate session reports and resource
metrics into workflow/handoffs/<task>.md;
|Human owner|
:Resolve findings; authorise commits on a named branch;
|Commit/PR agent|
:Group authorised changes into scoped
Conventional Commits; draft PR text;
|Human owner|
:Review commits; push and open PR;
:Cross-review by the other developer; merge;
stop
@enduml
